# {{ title }}

:::warning {title="Refused on purpose"}
Every block below is refused, and each one shows the diagnostic it produces in the Problems panel.
:::

Opening or previewing a document must never change data, read data outside its folder, or hang the editor. These examples show what YAMD refuses.

## Restricted Mode

In an untrusted workspace, no query runs and no database file is read. Every block shows "Queries are disabled in Restricted Mode".

## Folder scope (Y951)

A note can only use databases in its own folder or below it. The `outside` alias in the front matter points to a parent folder, so it is refused:

::db[outside]

Paths that climb out are refused too:

::db[../05-kanban/data/roadmap.ydb]

## Read-only queries (Y950)

Document queries can only read. A write is refused before it runs:

```query {db=tasks}
DELETE FROM tasks WHERE Status = 'Done'
```

Only one statement is allowed, so this can't sneak a write in after a read:

```query {db=crm}
SELECT 1; DROP TABLE contacts
```

Statements that reach other files or change settings are blocked:

```query {db=crm}
ATTACH '/etc/passwd' AS secrets
```

```query {db=crm}
PRAGMA writable_schema = ON
```

## Filter injection (Y950)

A filter is wrapped in a read-only query, so this can't delete anything:

::db[tasks]{filter="1=1); DELETE FROM tasks; --"}

## Time limit (Y952)

Queries stop after 2 seconds:

```query {db=tasks}
WITH RECURSIVE forever(n) AS (SELECT 1 UNION ALL SELECT n + 1 FROM forever)
SELECT count(*) FROM forever
```

## Data is always text

If a value contains HTML, it is shown as text, never run. Even this query only produces a harmless string:

```query {db=tasks}
SELECT '<img src=x onerror=alert(1)>' AS Payload
```

## Writes

Edits made in the preview are fixed operations, such as "set this cell", with values passed as parameters. A value like `x'); DROP TABLE tasks; --` is stored exactly as typed. The first write to a SQLite file in each session asks for permission, and every write is logged in the **YAMD Databases** output channel.
